---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CopyEmail from '../components/CopyEmail.astro';
import { link } from '../lib/links';

const updated = '23 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — MacAway"
  description="What MacAway keeps, where it keeps it, and why nothing leaves your Mac. Today's app contains no networking code at all."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="doc-head">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          This describes MacAway as it is built today and this website as it is served today.
          It will be rewritten before anything is released, and the date below will say so.
        </p>
        <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>The app collects nothing and sends nothing. It contains no networking code.</li>
          <li>It asks for one permission: Bluetooth.</li>
          <li>It never stores, reads or types your password. It locks; you unlock.</li>
          <li>
            This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. GitHub, which hosts it, keeps
            its own server logs.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the app keeps, and where</h2>
        <p>
          Everything MacAway remembers is in its own settings on your Mac, in the usual place
          macOS keeps an app&rsquo;s preferences. It is readable by you and by anything else
          running as you, and it goes when you remove the app&rsquo;s settings.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The devices you chose to follow.</strong> For each one: the name macOS
            already gives it, and the identifier CoreBluetooth assigns to it on this Mac. That
            identifier is local to this Mac &mdash; it is not a serial number and it means
            nothing on another machine.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Which sensitivity setting is chosen</strong>, and any numbers you changed
            under Advanced.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Whether MacAway is paused</strong>, and until when.</li>
          <li><strong>Whether it launches at login.</strong></li>
          <li>
            <strong>A journal of locks, kept for one week.</strong> Each entry holds the time,
            which device caused the lock, the reason, the signal reading, the numbers in force
            at the time, and your answer if you told MacAway whether that lock was wrong.
            Entries older than a week are dropped.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>None of it is sent anywhere, because there is nowhere for it to be sent to.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The one permission</h2>
        <p>
          Bluetooth, and nothing else. The prompt macOS shows says: &ldquo;MacAway uses
          Bluetooth to measure how close your iPhone or Apple Watch is, so it can lock this Mac
          when you walk away from it.&rdquo; MacAway uses the Bluetooth link to read signal
          strength, once a second, and that is the whole of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          It does not ask for, and does not use, the camera, the microphone, location
          services, your contacts, Accessibility or Full Disk Access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your password</h2>
        <p>
          MacAway locks the screen. It has no way to unlock it, and it contains no code that
          reads, stores or types a password. Locking and unlocking are not symmetrical here on
          purpose: an app that can put your password back is an app that has to hold it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Diagnostic logs</h2>
        <p>
          macOS keeps its own log of what the apps on your Mac are doing. MacAway writes to it
          &mdash; what it measured, why it locked &mdash; which is how a problem gets diagnosed.
          That log lives on your Mac and is rotated by macOS. Nothing in it is sent anywhere.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Updates and licensing</h2>
        <p>
          Neither is built. Today&rsquo;s app never connects to anything at all. Two things are
          planned, and both would change the sentence above, so both are written here before
          they exist rather than after:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Automatic updates.</strong> The app would check an update feed for a newer
            version. That is a request to that feed and nothing else.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>A paid licence.</strong> The plan is an offline key, checked on your Mac,
            with no server involved and no activation call.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This notice describes what exists. It will be updated before either of those ships,
          not afterwards.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>This website</h2>
        <p>
          The page you are reading is a set of static files served by GitHub Pages. It sets no
          cookies, runs no analytics, embeds nothing from anyone else, and has no sign-up form.
          The typeface is served from this site rather than from a font network, so loading
          this page tells no third party that you visited.
        </p>
        <p>
          GitHub logs the IP addresses of visitors to Pages sites and keeps them for a limited
          period to keep the service secure and to deal with abuse. Those logs are GitHub&rsquo;s,
          not ours, and are covered by <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
            >GitHub&rsquo;s privacy statement</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
        <div class="tbd">
          <span class="tbd-tag">To be supplied by the owner</span>
          <p>
            The name of the person or company responsible for this site and for MacAway goes
            here. This placeholder is deliberate: inventing it would be worse than leaving the
            section visibly unfinished, and this notice is not final until it is filled in.
          </p>
          <p>
            Write to the address below. That is a placeholder too, and the mailbox behind it
            is not set up yet.
          </p>
          <CopyEmail />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          The app holds no personal data of yours anywhere but on your own Mac, where it is
          already yours to read and to delete, and it has no account attached to you. That
          leaves the website&rsquo;s server logs, which GitHub holds as the host. Once the
          contact address above is working, you can use it to ask about any of this.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p>
          When it changes, the date at the top changes with it. There is no mailing list to
          announce it on, because there is no mailing list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="back"><a class="text-link" href={link('')}>&larr; Back to MacAway</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    padding-block: clamp(6rem, 10vw, 8rem) clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .doc :global(.wrap) > * {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .doc-head {
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .doc-head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 3.75rem);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .doc section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .doc p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .doc ul {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .doc ul.plain {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .doc ul.plain li {
    padding-left: 1.6rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .doc ul.plain li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62em;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--green-deep);
  }

  .doc strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 620;
  }

  .doc a {
    color: var(--green-deep);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .tbd {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .tbd-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .tbd p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .back {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .text-link {
    color: var(--green-deep);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .text-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
